    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d364">

                <pb facs="0433" n="415" sameAs="frus:frus1946v11/pg415"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.24112 RP/11–946: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Ambassador in Bolivia</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Flack</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-11-15T19:00:00-05:00">November 15, 1946—7
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>613. Urtel 1052, Nov. 9. New Bol int[erest] replacement program gratifying. List
                        Bol spearheads being reviewed for possible
                    elimination less serious cases. Dept would appreciate info re firms Bol wish to drop so
                    that it may comment before final action. Dept also studying <pb facs="0434"
                        n="416" xml:id="pg416"/> Peru decree Sept 3 for effect similar Bol decree would have on expropriation spearheads
                    and on Eisner and Kyllmann transfers. Your comments on latter point are
                    requested. Dept will discuss fully on recpt text draft decree.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
